        "original_id": "3577156c-df4f-564b-aae1-3816791ae8b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Manhattan Community Board 6\n- Places: Gramercy Park, Stuyvesant Town, Peter Cooper Village, Waterside Plaza, Murray Hill, Kips Bay, Turtle Bay, Tudor City, Sutton Place, Manhattan, East 34th Street, East 40th Street, Madison Avenue, East River\n- Topics: neighborhood boundaries, residential skyscraper complexes\n\nFacts:\n- Manhattan Community Board 6 includes the neighborhoods of Gramercy Park, Stuyvesant Town, Peter Cooper Village, Waterside Plaza, Murray Hill, Kips Bay, Turtle Bay, Tudor City, and Sutton Place.\n- Tudor City began construction in 1927 and was the first residential skyscraper complex in the world.\n- In 1999, Manhattan Community Board 6 defined Murray Hill's boundaries as East 34th Street on the south, East 40th Street on the north, Madison Avenue on the west, and the East River on the east.",
